WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.080
Just when you thought Marvel couldn't get
any more secretive, a story like this comes

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:04.780
out.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:09.140
One Avengers: Endgame actor had no idea they
were even in the movie, only realizing they

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.300
were a part of the super-sized superhero flick
when they saw it in theaters.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.000
The gobsmacked actor in question?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.180
Community alum Yvette Nicole Brown, who made
a cameo appearance at the S.H.I.E.L.D. base

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.480
Tony Stark and Steve Rogers visit in the 1970s.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:25.900
The trio share an elevator together during
a scene in which Brown's character, a S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.610
employee, becomes highly suspicious of the
two time-traveling Avengers during their last-ditch

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.850
effort to retrieve the Tesseract and a few
extra Pym Particles.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.850
Her suspicions eventually lead S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.780
higher-ups to try and thwart their mission.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.260
"You new here?"

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.620
"Not exactly."

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.660
As Brown explained in an interview with CNN,
she knew she was shooting her scenes for a

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.540
Marvel movie, but she didn't know which one
she would be in.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:54.340
When she saw Infinity War up on the big screen
and realized that she wasn't in it, Brown

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.720
assumed directors Joe and Anthony Russo had
simply scrapped her cameo.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.640
But it turns out, that wasn't the case.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:04.620
It all started in October of 2017, two months
after principal photography began on Infinity

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.260
War.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:09.240
Joe Russo reached out to Brown and asked if
she was available to film some scenes.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.160
Brown recalled,

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.740
"I was on the set of The Mayor for ABC and
I got a text from Joe Russo.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.560
He said, 'Hey, what are you doing two weeks
from now?'...He said, 'This is it.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:18.420
It's your turn.'"

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:23.140
Because Marvel and ABC both operate under
the Disney umbrella, Brown was able to reconfigure

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:27.329
her schedule, traveling to Atlanta for a couple
of days to knock out her MCU appearance.

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:31.939
With her fellow Community cast members Danny
Pudi, Jim Rash, and Ken Jeong having already

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:36.340
snagged cameos in Marvel movies, Brown jumped
at the opportunity to join the MCU.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:41.299
She was also keen to reunite with the Russos,
who worked as executive producers on Community

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.440
before being called up to Marvel's big leagues.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.160
She said,

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.300
"I don't dream that big.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.480
[But] after the Russos took over, I thought,
'There's a good chance.'

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.260
There's a lot of people on Community, and
there's not enough movies for everybody to

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:55.090
have a moment, so I was so excited that I
got my chance."

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:58.909
Brown recalls enjoying her time on set, as
well as her experience filming a scene with

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:02.340
Downey Jr. and Evans, whom she called lovely
human beings.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:05.840
But she walked away not knowing exactly what
movie she'd filmed a scene for.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.900
Assuming that she'd probably pop up in Infinity
War, Brown was a bit let down when she didn't

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:14.020
see herself up on the silver screen, but still
felt grateful to have been a part of the production.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:14.980
According to Brown,

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.500
"I just said, 'Well, it was nice.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.850
It's the thought that counts.'

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:18.740
And I forgot about it."

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:23.880
She got the shock of her life in April 2019,
a year and a half after she stepped onto set,

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.200
when she sat down for a showing of Avengers:
Endgame.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.780
When the action shifted to the S.H.I.E.L.D.
base, Brown knew that her time to shine had

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:30.790
finally come.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:33.900
"I'm sitting there with a group of [friends]
in my seat like, 'This is going to be it.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.420
Oh my God, it's an elevator!

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:36.220
It's me!'"

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.020
She later admitted the one regret she has
about the whole experience: not going to the

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:41.190
Endgame premiere.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:45.110
While it's unusual for an actor to not know
they're in a film until they see it in theaters,

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:47.440
this doesn't feel too shocking coming out
of Marvel.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.760
The studio has gotten increasingly secretive
over the years, and has garnered a reputation

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.260
for keeping things close to the chest - especially
in regards to Infinity War and Endgame.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.900
The filmmakers and marketers purposefully
misdirected fans with misleading trailer edits,

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:04.220
and distributed fake scripts for the actors
filled with phony twists.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:07.760
There were even moments when the filmmakers
straight-up lied to the performers about the

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.420
context of scenes they were shooting.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:13.400
It was all done for the sake of preventing
spoilers from spilling out, which thankfully

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.080
didn't happen that often - the occasional
Mark Ruffalo reveal notwithstanding.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.120
"I get impulsive sometimes..."

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:23.600
Of course, Brown is hardly the first or only
actor to film something for Marvel without

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.220
knowing exactly what it was for.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:29.560
She's joined by Captain Marvel herself, Brie
Larson, who filmed scenes for Avengers: Endgame

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:34.020
without knowing, she says, much of anything
about her character or role in the story.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:38.920
"It wasn't until I walked on set that I was
like 'Oh, crap.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.840
I'm, like, in a Marvel movie right now.'"

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:47.600
It's a similar story for Pepper Potts actor
Gwyneth Paltrow, who made a special appearance

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:51.690
in Spider-Man: Homecoming before later swearing
up and down that she wasn't in the movie - at

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.360
least, not that she could remember.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:54.720
"Spider-Man?"

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.100
"Yeah, we were in Spider-Man, again.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.220
Remember when we were on Spider-Man?"

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.120
"We weren't in Spider-Man."

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.120
"Yes we were."

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.200
While it was apparently standard procedure
to keep actors oblivious to the specifics

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.160
of the third and fourth Avengers movies, the
Russos didn't have anything to worry about

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.380
when it comes to Brown.

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:13.480
She confirmed to CNN that she zipped her lips
immediately after filming her scenes - and

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.560
kept them that way for nearly two years.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:16.860
According to the actress,

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.400
"That NDA was iron-clad.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.140
I never told anybody."

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:23.400
The result was an appearance that wasn't just
a surprise to her friends.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.160
It was a surprise to her, too.

